Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Current Patch Set: &lt;br/&gt;
Commit: fa272655911223cd39536c537380699659be7095&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="494710" author="JIRAUSER19288" created="Mon, 18 May 2026 09:29:25 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Merged for 2.18&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="499567" author="sebastien" created="Thu, 13 Aug 2026 16:07:40 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=ckansal&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;ckansal&quot;&gt;ckansal&lt;/a&gt; it looks like it does not work on the default nodemap, when the rbac property is previously set to &apos;all&apos;?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;[~]&amp;gt; lctl nodemap_modify --name default --property rbac --value all
[~]&amp;gt; lctl get_param nodemap.default.rbac
nodemap.default.rbac=file_perms,dne_ops,quota_ops,byfid_ops,chlg_ops,fscrypt_admin,server_upcall,ignore_root_prjquota,hsm_ops,immutable_flags,pool_quota_ops,lqa_quota_ops,projid_set,foreign_ops
[~]&amp;gt; lctl nodemap_modify --name default --property rbac --value -projid_set
error: invalid ioctl: 000ce05f errno: 22: Invalid argument
error: nodemap_modify: cannot modify nodemap &apos;default&apos; to param &apos;rbac&apos;: value &apos;-projid_set&apos;: Invalid argument
[~]&amp;gt; lctl get_param nodemap.default.rbac
nodemap.default.rbac=file_perms,dne_ops,quota_ops,byfid_ops,chlg_ops,fscrypt_admin,server_upcall,ignore_root_prjquota,hsm_ops,immutable_flags,pool_quota_ops,lqa_quota_ops,projid_set,foreign_ops
[~]&amp;gt; lctl nodemap_modify --name default --property rbac --value file_perms,dne_ops,quota_ops,projid_set,foreign_ops
[~]&amp;gt; lctl get_param nodemap.default.rbac
nodemap.default.rbac=file_perms,dne_ops,quota_ops,projid_set,foreign_ops
[~]&amp;gt; lctl nodemap_modify --name default --property rbac --value -projid_set
[~]&amp;gt; lctl get_param nodemap.default.rbac
nodemap.default.rbac=file_perms,dne_ops,quota_ops,foreign_ops
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="499659" author="JIRAUSER19503" created="Sat, 15 Aug 2026 06:56:54 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;rbac=all is stored as NODEMAP_RBAC_ALL (0xFFFFFFFF), which also includes local_admin. Although local_admin is not valid for the default nodemap, get_param hides this bit.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For an update like -file_perms, the stored all mask is used, file_perms is cleared, but local_admin remains set. Since the mask is no longer all, nodemap_set_rbac() rejects it for the default nodemap.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="499702" author="gerrit" created="Mon, 17 Aug 2026 07:04:56 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&quot;Chakshu Kansal &amp;lt;ckansal@ddn.com&amp;gt;&quot; uploaded a new patch: &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68039&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68039&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
